---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson 18</p>
  <h1>Weather &amp; <em>seasons</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Talk about the sky and the year. Describe the weather with <strong>It's + adjective</strong> — <span class="ex">It's sunny.</span> — or with <strong>It's + verb-ing</strong> for rain and snow — <span class="ex">It's raining.</span> Name the four seasons and say when things happen with <span class="ex">in summer</span>, <span class="ex">in winter</span>.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 45–55 min</span>
    <span class="tag">It's + adjective / -ing</span>
    <span class="tag">spring · summer · fall · winter</span>
    <span class="tag">8 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Compare two ways to talk about weather.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Adjective or -ing? Plus the four seasons.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Match, choose, and build chunks.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Describe today, your seasons, your plans.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">American English uses <span class="ex">fall</span> for the season between summer and winter. British English uses <span class="ex">autumn</span> for the same season — both are correct; we'll use <span class="ex">fall</span> here.</p>

  <h2>Meet the weather</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>We describe the weather with <span class="ex">It's…</span> + a weather word: <span class="ex">It's sunny. It's rainy today.</span></p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/sunny.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">sunny</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/cloudy.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">cloudy</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/rainy.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">rainy</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/stormy.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">stormy</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/snowy.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">snowy</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/windy.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">windy</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/foggy.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">foggy</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/rainbow.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">rainbow</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/lightning.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">lightning</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/fire.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">hot</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/snowflake.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">cold</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Meet the seasons</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The year has four seasons. We use <span class="ex">in</span> with a season: <span class="ex">in summer, in winter.</span></p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/spring.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">spring</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/summer.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">summer</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/fall.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">fall</span></div>
    <div class="figure"><span class="fig"><img src="/assets/lessons/img/noto/winter.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></span><span class="nm">winter</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Two ways to talk about the sky</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"It's sunny today, so I'll walk to work. Wait — now it's raining. It's cold and windy too, so I'll take the bus."</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Look at <span class="ex">It's sunny</span> and <span class="ex">It's cold</span>. What kind of word comes after <strong>It's</strong> — a describing word, or an action?</li>
      <li>Now look at <span class="ex">It's raining</span>. This one is an <strong>action</strong> happening now. How does the word <span class="ex">rain</span> change?</li>
      <li>So there are two patterns. One uses a describing word; the other uses a verb with <span class="ex">-ing</span>. Which words go in which group?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check — adjective or action?</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">If the word describes the day, it's an <b>adjective</b>. If it's an action happening now, it ends in <b>-ing</b>.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="sunny">sunny</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="cold">cold</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="raining">raining</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="snowing">snowing</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>It's <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="sunny" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(adjective · the sun is out)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>It's <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="raining" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(action now · water is falling)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>It's <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="cold" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(adjective · low temperature)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>It's <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="snowing" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(action now · snow is falling)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: two patterns, four seasons</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>When you ask about the weather, the natural question is:</p>
  <p><span class="ex">What's the weather like?</span> &nbsp;→&nbsp; <span class="ex">It's sunny.</span> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <span class="ex">It's raining.</span></p>
  <p><strong>1. It's + adjective</strong> describes the day. Most weather words work this way:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>adjective</th><th>meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>sunny</b></td><td>the sun is out</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>cloudy</b></td><td>gray sky, clouds, no sun</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>windy</b></td><td>a lot of wind</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>foggy</b></td><td>thick mist; hard to see far</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>hot · warm · cool · cold</b></td><td>temperature, from high to low</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>humid</b></td><td>hot and very wet in the air</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><strong>2. It's + verb-ing</strong> says an action is happening now. We use this for falling weather:</p>
  <p><span class="ex">It's raining.</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <span class="ex">It's snowing.</span> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <span class="ex">The sun is shining.</span></p>
  <p>Note the pairs: the action <span class="ex">It's raining</span> matches the adjective <span class="ex">It's rainy</span>; <span class="ex">It's snowing</span> matches <span class="ex">It's snowy</span>.</p>
  <p>The year has four <strong>seasons</strong>. Say when something happens with <strong>in + season</strong>:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>season</th><th>typical weather</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>spring</b></td><td>cool, often rainy</td><td><span class="ex">In spring it's often rainy.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>summer</b></td><td>hot, sunny</td><td><span class="ex">In summer it's hot.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>fall</b> <span class="contraction">autumn</span></td><td>cool, windy</td><td><span class="ex">In fall it's windy.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>winter</b></td><td>cold, snowy</td><td><span class="ex">In winter it's cold.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Meaning check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Can we say <span class="ex">It's rain</span>? <strong>No.</strong> Use the adjective <span class="ex">It's rainy</span>, or the action <span class="ex">It's raining</span> — never the bare word <span class="ex">rain</span> after <span class="ex">It's</span>.</li>
      <li>Do we say <span class="ex">on summer</span> or <span class="ex">at summer</span>? <strong>No.</strong> For seasons we use <span class="ex">in</span>: <span class="ex">in summer</span>, <span class="ex">in winter</span>.</li>
      <li>What's the difference between <span class="ex">warm</span> and <span class="ex">hot</span>? <strong>Warm</strong> is pleasant, mild heat; <strong>hot</strong> is a high, strong temperature.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose the right pattern</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The cue in brackets tells you whether you need a describing word or an action. Keep the chunk together: <span class="ex">It's + word</span>.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1 — adjective or -ing?</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">A describing word stays plain; a falling-weather action ends in <b>-ing</b></p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="windy">windy</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="raining">raining</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="snowing">snowing</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="cloudy">cloudy</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="hot">hot</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="foggy">foggy</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Take an umbrella — it's <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="raining" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(action · water falling)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Hold your hat — it's very <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="windy" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(adjective · a lot of wind)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Drive slowly — it's <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="foggy" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> on the road. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(adjective · hard to see)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The roads are white — it's <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="snowing" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(action · snow falling)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>No sun today — it's gray and <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="cloudy" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(adjective · full of clouds)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Drink water — it's 35 degrees and <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="hot" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(adjective · high temperature)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Match the season to its weather</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game>
    <h3>Drill 2 — match each season to its typical weather</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap a season, then tap the weather that fits it</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="summer">summer</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="winter">winter</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="spring">spring</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="fall">fall</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="summer" data-placeholder="hot and sunny">hot and sunny</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="winter" data-placeholder="cold and snowy">cold and snowy</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="spring" data-placeholder="cool, with a lot of rain">cool, with a lot of rain</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="fall" data-placeholder="cool and windy, leaves fall">cool and windy, leaves fall</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the weather sentence</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="it's sunny today">
    <h3>Drill 3 — build the sentence</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">The sun is out this morning. Build the sentence, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="today">today</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="it's">It's</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="sunny">sunny</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="it's raining outside">
    <h3>Drill 4 — build the action sentence</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Rain is falling right now. Use the <span class="ex">-ing</span> action form.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="raining">raining</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="it's">It's</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="outside">outside</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="rain" data-fix="It's raining today." data-why="After It's we need an adjective (rainy) or an action (raining), never the bare word rain. The action form is raining.">
    <h3>Drill 5 — fix the weather word</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong. Rain is falling now.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="it's">It's</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="rain">rain</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="today">today.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="on" data-fix="In summer it's hot." data-why="For seasons we use the preposition in, not on. We say in summer, in winter.">
    <h3>Drill 6 — fix the preposition</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="on">On</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="summer">summer</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="it's">it's</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="hot">hot.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 7 — say the weather, then reveal</h3>
    <p>Read the cue and say the full sentence aloud first. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> the sun is out &nbsp;→&nbsp; It's + adjective</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>It's sunny.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> snow is falling now &nbsp;→&nbsp; It's + -ing</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>It's snowing.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> a lot of wind today &nbsp;→&nbsp; It's + adjective</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>It's windy.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> water is falling now &nbsp;→&nbsp; It's + -ing</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>It's raining.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> the season after summer, it's windy &nbsp;→&nbsp; In + season…</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>In fall it's windy.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>The week’s forecast</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“Quick forecast for the week: Monday is sunny and warm. On Tuesday it’s cloudy, and on Wednesday it rains all day. It’s windy on Thursday. The weekend looks perfect, sunny with a clear sky.”</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You understood a real weather forecast.">
    <h3>Read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="rainy">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. What is the weather on Wednesday?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="rainy">rainy</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="sunny">sunny</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="windy">windy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Thursday">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. Which day is windy?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Thursday">Thursday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Monday">Monday</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Tuesday">Tuesday</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="sunny">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. How is the weekend?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="sunny">sunny</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="cloudy">cloudy</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="rainy">rainy</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>The weather today:</b> Look outside and describe the weather where you live right now in two or three sentences. <span class="ex">It's cloudy and cool. It's not raining.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your favorite season:</b> Say which season you like best and why, using <span class="ex">in + season</span>. <span class="ex">I like summer best. In summer it's hot and sunny, and I travel.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Weather and plans:</b> Pair the weather with an activity. <span class="ex">It's sunny, so I'll walk to work. It's snowing, so I'll stay home.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Small talk:</b> Practice the opener with the teacher. <span class="ex">What's the weather like there today? — It's warm and windy.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Pack a bag:</b> The teacher names a season or weather; you say one thing to wear or bring. <span class="ex">It's rainy → I'll take an umbrella. In winter → I'll wear a coat.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the two patterns back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “To describe the day I say <strong>It's</strong> + a describing word, like <span class="ex">It's ______</span>. For rain and snow happening now I say <strong>It's</strong> + a word ending in ______, like <span class="ex">It's ______</span>. For seasons I use the preposition ______.”</p>
    <p>Then say one true sentence about the weather right now and one about your favorite season.</p>
  </div>

